cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, its battery models, estimation algorithms,
  or results obtained with this framework in scientific or academic work,
  please cite this repository.

title: "BEAST: Battery Estimation Architecture and Simulation Toolkit"
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Dello Iacono"
    given-names: "Salvatore"
    affiliation: "Università degli Studi di Brescia"

abstract: >-
  BEAST (Battery Estimation Architecture and Simulation Toolkit) is a Python framework
  for battery modeling and state estimation. The project originates from work
  developed for a Bachelor's Degree Thesis and subsequent Undergraduate
  Research activities on battery modeling, state estimation, and embedded
  Battery Management Systems at the Università degli Studi di Salerno.
  The current Python implementation evolves earlier MATLAB, C++, and FPGA/Nios II
  implementations into a structured NumPy-based research software framework.

keywords:
  - batteries
  - battery modeling
  - battery management system
  - BMS
  - state of charge
  - SoC
  - state of health
  - SoH
  - extended Kalman filter
  - dual EKF
  - Mix Algorithm
  - lithium-ion battery
  - Python
  - NumPy

